# Normalise line endings in the repository. Evidence records and hashes are
# computed over in-memory values, never over files, so this is hygiene rather
# than correctness — but a chain fixture that differs by line ending between
# platforms would be an unpleasant way to learn that.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary

# The frozen conformance fixture is hashed byte for byte by
# `tests/evidence/test_frozen_format.py`, so its line endings are not hygiene
# here -- they are part of the pinned digest. LF in the repository and LF on
# every checkout, which is what `* text=auto eol=lf` above already gives; this
# line is here so that anyone changing that rule sees what depends on it. The
# generator writes bytes rather than text for the same reason: `write_text` on
# Windows would have produced CRLF and a digest that matched on one machine.
tests/evidence/fixtures/evidence-format-*/** text eol=lf
